@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.3.3
@changelog
  - Codename: Almost, but not quite, entirely unlike tea.
  - Docs: the manual is current with the shipped build again (it still described v0.2). New chapters for Sends and Receives, dynamic soft-key sub-banks, Hardware Modes, DynaMount, Stream Deck and Companion; Favourites rewritten for the CS + BC model; ~20 stale claims corrected. Readable in Settings -> Manual.
  - Docs: DynaMount axes were documented inverted — the fader is X, FLIP is Y. The in-app footer was always right.
  - Docs: the Stream Deck plugin hard-codes 127.0.0.1:49900, so it cannot follow a moved bridge port and the LAN bind does nothing for it. Now stated in streamdeck/README.md.
  - Fix: the MCP Inserts overlay highlight lands on the right insert. It now reads the mixer's own row labels instead of counting rows, so empty FX slots and grouped plug-in parameters no longer push it onto the wrong row.
  - Fix: toggling "show FX parameters" now moves the overlay highlight live — it previously stayed wrong until you changed track.
